&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8912&quot; title=&quot;PartitionLossPolicy.READ_ONLY_SAFE does not detect partition loss &quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-8912&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-8912&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; PartitionLossPolicy.READ_ONLY_SAFE does not detect partition loss&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16537949" author="pvinokurov" created="Tue, 10 Jul 2018 03:38:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=slava.koptilin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;slava.koptilin&quot;&gt;slava.koptilin&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, Please look at the patch. The main question is to should we mark partition as lost in GridDhtPartitionTopologyImpl#afterExchange method and duplicate logic located in detectLostPartitions()&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16538902" author="pvinokurov" created="Tue, 10 Jul 2018 16:31:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I removed changing state for MOVING partition if all owners left topology in GridDhtPartitionTopologyImpl#afterExchange  method. If an owner node left cluster during exchange, then new exchange should be scheduled with detecting lost partitions. So It isn&apos;t necessary to detect lost partition and raise event in GridDhtPartitionTopologyImpl#afterExchange. &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=slava.koptilin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;slava.koptilin&quot;&gt;slava.koptilin&lt;/a&gt; Does it make sense?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16538971" author="slava.koptilin" created="Tue, 10 Jul 2018 17:14:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pvinokurov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pvinokurov&quot;&gt;pvinokurov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
It seems to me, your changes look correct.&lt;br/&gt;
At the moment when `GridDhtPartitionTopologyImpl.afterExchange()` is called, the `exchange` process is already completed,&lt;br/&gt;
and so I can imagine one possible situation when we have a partition in the `MOVING` state and there is no owner. Owner node left the cluster and `discoCache` was updated by `discovery` thread, and as you mentioned, new exchange will mark that partition as lost.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16539719" author="pvinokurov" created="Wed, 11 Jul 2018 08:30:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt; Please review&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16539890" author="agoncharuk" created="Wed, 11 Jul 2018 10:49:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks good to me given that TC passes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16540150" author="pvinokurov" created="Wed, 11 Jul 2018 14:16:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt; TC results look good.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16543445" author="agoncharuk" created="Fri, 13 Jul 2018 17:06:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks, Pavel, merged your changes to master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
